  "question": {
    "text": "Frequency of the de-Broglie wave of electron in Bohr's first orbit of hydrogen atom is _______ \\(\\times 10^{13} \\mathrm{~Hz}\\) (nearest integer).\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { [Given : } \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{H}}(\\text { Rydberg constant })=2.18 \\times 10^{-18} \\mathrm{~J}, h \\text { (Plank's } \\\\\n& \\text { constant })=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~J} \\text {.s.] }\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "661",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\lambda=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{mv}} \\\\ & \\lambda=\\frac{\\mathrm{hv}}{\\mathrm{mv}^2} \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{mv}^2}{\\mathrm{~h}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}}{\\lambda}=\\mathrm{v} \\text { (frequency) } \\\\ & \\text { Given } \\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{mv}^2=2.18 \\times 10^{-18} \\mathrm{~J} \\\\ & \\mathrm{~h}=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\\\ & \\mathrm{v}=\\frac{4.36 \\times 10^{-18}}{6.6 \\times 10^{-34}}=660.60 \\times 10^{13} \\mathrm{~Hz} \\\\ & \\approx 661 \\times 10^{13} \\mathrm{~Hz}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
